The fun of engineering begins when you change someone else's example! 🛠️

Let's modify our starter sketch to display a two-line greeting for your robot:

```cpp
void setup() {
  lcd.init();
  lcd.backlight();

  // Line 1 (Top row)
  lcd.setCursor(0, 0);
  lcd.print("Monster: Sparky");

  // Line 2 (Bottom row)
  lcd.setCursor(0, 1);
  lcd.print("Status: ONLINE");
}
```

### Making Predictions
Notice the cursor coordinates: `lcd.setCursor(col, row)`. In computer programming, rows and columns start counting from **0**, not 1!
- `(0, 0)` is the very first character of the **top row**.
- `(0, 1)` is the very first character of the **bottom row**.

What happens if you change `"ONLINE"` to `"SLEEPING"`? The screen updates with your new word when you re-upload! By changing one line at a time, you learn how the library controls the physical world.
